---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import chase from '../assets/pets/chase-story.webp';
---

<Base
  title="Our Story"
  description="How a foster bull terrier named Chase, a Cape Town shelter and a dog called Molly became Sit Molly Sit!"
>
  <section class="section">
    <article class="container story">
      <h1>Our Story</h1>
      <div class="story__body stack" style="--stack: 1.1rem">
        <p>
          Chase came into my life as a foster through Adorabull, and he quickly proved why bull terriers are called
          “velcro dogs”: all heart, all in, always close. He was an absolute tank, a real alpha male, but what stayed with
          me most was how effortlessly gentle he was with people, including kids. When Chase passed away, it left a hole I
          still feel every day.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started volunteering at DARG in Cape Town, walking dogs and trying to do something useful with the grief. One
          day I set up a small photo shoot for a few of the animals, just to see if better photos could help them get
          adopted.
        </p>
        <p>
          One of the dogs in that first shoot was named Molly. Hearing her name took me straight back to a family dog I had
          as a kid, and it stuck with me. It’s where <em>Sit Molly Sit</em> comes from.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before long, people were asking if I could do the same for their own pets, and that accidental little idea
          became what we do today. Now we’re a small, passionate team obsessed with bringing your pets to life in portrait
          form. Premium quality without the hassle and cost of a traditional studio shoot. Chase is still the reason we
          care this much.
        </p>
        <p class="story__sign"><strong>Grant &amp; Chase</strong></p>
      </div>
      <Picture
        class="story__photo"
        src={chase}
        alt="Chase, a white bull terrier, sitting and smiling on a grey studio background"
        formats={['avif', 'webp']}
        widths={[400, 640, 900, 1200]}
        sizes="(min-width: 760px) 680px, 100vw"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .story {
    max-width: calc(42rem + 2 * var(--gutter));
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--fs-2xl);
  }
  .story__body {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .story__sign {
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .story :global(.story__photo) {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
